# ouroboros#197: a function's `x is 1` where module x is bound only in a
# branch that did NOT run. On the VM the store creates a call-local (no
# outer binding exists at call time), so the module read after the call
# dies "undefined variable 'x'". The AOT used to take the store outward
# and set the module boundness bit (printed 1). Now a function's plain
# store to a bit-carrying module name routes on the bit: outward if set,
# else into a call-local shadow that reads back inside the call.
define f() as:
    x is 1
    return x + 1
if 1 == 2:
    x is 5
print of (f of null)
print of x
